# Lessons Learned — Free Throw Frenzy

## Project Patterns
- CRA project bootstrapped with React 19; TypeScript added as a dependency.
- Game engine is pure TS with no React dependency for hot-loop performance.
- Canvas rendering and React HUD are separated; state flows via callbacks/refs.

## Preferences
- Minimal dependencies: no Phaser, Matter.js, or similar engines.
- Vector-only graphics (canvas arcs/rects) — no image assets for v1.
- Tailwind for all UI styling; no additional CSS frameworks.

## Known Challenges
- CRA + TypeScript requires renaming .js → .tsx and adding tsconfig.json.
- Mobile touch input needs `passive: false` for `touchstart` to prevent scroll.
- Canvas must resize responsively without losing aspect ratio.

## Decisions Log
| Date | Decision | Rationale |
|------|----------|-----------|
| 2026-08-19 | CRA over Vite | Project already bootstrapped with CRA |
| 2026-08-19 | Single canvas + React overlay | Simpler compositing, better perf |
| 2026-08-19 | Euler integration for physics | Simple, fast, sufficient for 2D ball arc |
| 2026-08-19 | solveArcVelocity over angle/speed formula | Exact math guarantees ball reaches target — old formula was broken |
| 2026-08-19 | Gravity 680 over 980 | More visible arcs, better gameplay feel |
| 2026-08-19 | Web Audio API synthesis over audio files | Zero assets, instant load, smaller bundle |
| 2026-08-19 | Cel-shading style | Multi-tone fills + dark outlines give cartoon look with pure canvas API |
| 2026-08-19 | Auto-fire at max power | Prevents exploit; callback pattern in updateCharge avoids extra state |
| 2026-08-19 | Ground bounce vs out-of-bounds | Separate checkGroundBounce before checkOutOfBounds; bounce count limits prevent infinite loops |
| 2026-08-19 | Utils must be in src/ | CRA enforces import boundary; all shared code goes in src/utils/ |
| 2026-08-19 | Shop persistence in localStorage | Separate keys for unlocked bgs, active bg, and coins; graceful fallback on error |
